-- title:
--   Invertibility of the vanishing ideal of η̄
-- statement:
--   Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme and let $\eta$ be a point of $Y$. Assume that the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{Y,\eta}$, the stalk of the structure presheaf at $\eta$, has Krull dimension exactly $1$, and that for every point $y$ in the closure $Z=\overline{\{\eta\}}$ of $\{\eta\}$ in $Y$ the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{Y,y}$ is a regular local ring of Krull dimension at most $2$. Let $\mathcal{I}_Z$ be the vanishing ideal sheaf data attached to the closed subset $Z$ (closed because it is a closure). The conclusion is that $\mathcal{I}_Z$ satisfies the predicate `IsInvertible`, which unfolds to the following: for every point $x$ of $Y$ there are an affine open $U\subseteq Y$ and a section $f\in\Gamma(Y,U)$ with $x$ lying in the basic open subset $Y.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with an element $g$ of $\Gamma(Y, Y.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ that is a non-zero-divisor and such that the ideal cut out by $\mathcal{I}_Z$ on the affine open $Y.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f$ is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Thus $Z$ is locally principal, generated by a non-zero-divisor, on a family of affine opens covering $Y$.
--
--   This is the statement that an irreducible closed subset which is the closure of a point of codimension one, all of whose points have regular stalks of dimension at most $2$, is an effective Cartier divisor — the form in which "Weil divisors are Cartier on a locally factorial scheme" is needed for arithmetic surfaces, where regularity is only assumed along the subset. It is used in the construction of resolved Deligne–Rapoport model packages and in the treatment of the components of the special fibre of the modular curve $X_1(p)$, where vertical divisors must be exhibited as invertible ideal sheaves.
